\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Through the night of doubt and sorrow,
\par Onward goes the pilgrim band,
\par Singing songs of expectation,
\par Marching to the promised land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Clear before us through the darkness
\par Gleams and burns the guiding light;
\par Brother clasps the hand of brother,
\par Stepping fearless through the night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Once the light of God's own presence,
\par O'er His ransomed people shed,
\par Chasing far the gloom and terror,
\par Brightening all the path we tread:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. One the object of our journey,
\par One the faith which never tires,
\par One the earnest looking forward,
\par One the hope our God inspires:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. One the strain that lips of thousands
\par Lift as from the heart of one;
\par One the conflict, one the peril,
\par One the march in God begun:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. One the gladness of rejoicing
\par On the far eternal shore,
\par Where the one almighty Father
\par Reigns in love for evermore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Onward therefore, pilgrim brothers,
\par Onward with the Cross our aid!
\par Bear its shame, and fight its battle,
\par Till we rest beneath its shade.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Soon shall come the great awaking,
\par Soon the rending of the tomb;
\par Then the scattering of all shadows,
\par And the end of toil and gloom.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

